==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[pro tempore]] - US Constitution, Amendment XXV (1967), Section 3.

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|la}} phrase; ''[[pro#Latin|pro]] [[tempus#Latin|tempore]]''. The proposition ''[[pro#Latin|pro]]'' means "[[for]]" and ''[[tempore#Latin|tempore]]'' is the {{ablative}} of ''[[tempus#Latin|tempus]]'' meaning "[[time]]".

===Adverb===
'''pro tem'''

# [[temporarily]]; for the time being

===Adjective===
'''pro tem'''

# [[temporary]]

